# Drafted by Gemini (side quests batch 3: hair), edited.

~ start
Narrator: The shop smells of bay rum and hot iron, though a sour sweat clings to the barber's collar.
randall_graham [smile]: Trim or a bloodletting, friends? Swept-up locks from my floor keep turning up in the undertaker's cellar, and I cannot fathom how.
* We will look into it. -> accept
* Why does it matter? -> why
* Not now. -> END

~ why
randall_graham [afraid]: Every lock down there belongs to a fellow who took a rattling chill the week after his trim. Folk are eyeing my scissors crooked.
-> start

~ accept
randall_graham [weary]: Bless your boots. Have a poke around my cellar stairs if you like, or down at Mori's place.
quest hair_of_the_dog asked
set hair_asked
-> END

~ clue_barber
Narrator: Behind a crate of tonic bottles sits a glass jar stuffed with ribboned hair and paper slips.
* [Investigation DC 12] Read the labels and the dates. -> clue_barber_ok | clue_barber_fail

~ clue_barber_ok
Narrator: Each slip bears a customer's name and a dark-moon date, matching the Order's monthly tithe.
set hair_clue_a
-> END

~ clue_barber_fail
Narrator: Cellar rot and tallow ink have blurred the dates. The pattern may show clearer at the funeral home.
-> END

~ clue_funeral
Narrator: Beside an unchiseled coffin plate rests a jar of hair, tied with the same barber's twine.
set hair_clue_b
-> END

~ confront
Narrator: Randall's razor clatters into the porcelain basin, his round face gone the colour of mutton fat.
randall_graham [afraid]: Do not say it aloud! I owed the Order a steep sum from a bad winter, and they took payment in clippings. I swear I never knew why.
* Offer to pay the debt (fifty gold). -> pay_debt
* [Persuasion DC 12] Tell him to confess to Doris. -> confess_ok | confess_fail
* Keep his secret. -> keep

~ pay_debt
randall_graham [weary]: Fifty coin, just like that? You have lifted a millstone off my windpipe. I will sweep my floor straight into the stove from now on.
gold -50
set hair_outcome = "paid"
quest hair_of_the_dog done
standing cult +1
-> END

~ confess_ok
randall_graham [sad]: You are right. Better Doris Squire's iron look than waking up in a cold sweat every bell.
Narrator: At the barracks door, Doris only sighs and sets the kettle on, gentle as forged steel.
set hair_outcome = "confessed"
quest hair_of_the_dog done
standing old_ways +1
-> END

~ confess_fail
randall_graham [afraid]: To Doris? Have you seen the woman's eyes? My knees would turn to broth before I reached the jailhouse steps.
-> confront

~ keep
randall_graham [sly]: Mum's the word, then. Take these coins and a curl from my own crown, so we are bound fair and square.
set hair_outcome = "kept"
quest hair_of_the_dog done
gold +15
-> END
